# The clockwise square: mirror of square.tour (same 700 mm sides, same
# two planned stops on opposite legs) with every turn NEGATIVE omega.
#
# Why it exists: the rotation calibration carries SEPARATE gains for
# positive and negative turns (rotation_gain_pos / rotation_gain_neg), so
# a CCW-only square can never see a per-direction asymmetry. Run both
# squares; compare their closures.

MARK leg1a
TWIST vx=150 dist=350 timeout=9
STOP dwell=1.0
MARK leg1b
TWIST vx=150 dist=350 timeout=9
TWIST omega=-45 angle=90 timeout=8

MARK leg2
TWIST vx=150 dist=700 timeout=15
TWIST omega=-45 angle=90 timeout=8

MARK leg3a
TWIST vx=150 dist=350 timeout=9
STOP dwell=1.0
MARK leg3b
TWIST vx=150 dist=350 timeout=9
TWIST omega=-45 angle=90 timeout=8

MARK leg4
TWIST vx=150 dist=700 timeout=15
TWIST omega=-45 angle=90 timeout=8
STOP dwell=0.5

SEND STATUS
EXPECT '.type=="cleartext" and .verb=="STATUS" and .payload.ready==1' timeout=2.0
CAMFIX x=0 y=0 radius=80
